@startuml critical_position_flow
title Influence-surface flow: find the worst IRC:6 vehicle position

|models|
start
:BridgeInput + DeckCrossSection;

|builder|
:build_bridge_model
(mesh.build_mesh + assembly);
note right: nodes, shells, girders,\nbracing, supports in OpenSees

|analysis|
:InfluenceSolver(model.as_deck_model());
:for_girder_moment / for_deflection / for_truss_axial;

|solver|
:OpenSeesBackend.solve_with_loads(adjoint loads);

|analysis|
:InfluenceSurface\n(deflected shape = response everywhere);
:rank_all_positions(surface, cross_section, span_m);

|irc6|
:vehicles_allowed_in_each_block\n(irc6.vehicles);

|analysis|
:VehicleResponses → find_worst_train\n(along_span);
:envelope_every_block → find_worst_placement\n(across_carriageway);

|irc6|
if (apply_footway_load?) then (yes)
  :footway_response (irc6.lanes);
else (no)
endif

|analysis|
:centre_the_resultant\n(resultant_centring);
:describe → CriticalPosition + VehiclePlacement\n(results);
:find_critical_position = first of the ranked list;
stop
@enduml
